course: dictionary
lesson: 3805
title: The forehead in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your forehead is the part of your face above your eyes and below your hair. Words about the forehead can tell you a lot about how someone feels, so read the clues around them.
explain: Writers use the forehead to show feelings. «Sweat on his forehead» can show heat, fear or hard work. A wrinkled forehead can show worry or deep thinking, and you can see it in a face without anyone saying a word.
explain: Context also tells you where a body part is. «A helmet should sit level and low on your forehead, about two fingers above your eyebrows.» The clue is above your eyebrows, so the forehead is the space between your eyebrows and your hair.
fact: Your forehead is the part of your face above your eyes and below your hair.
fact: A hot forehead can be a sign of a fever, so grown-ups often feel a child's forehead to check.
fact: Some thermometers are pointed at the forehead to read body temperature.
fact: «Kowtow» comes from Chinese for "knock head", a deep bow touching the forehead to the ground.
fact: A coot is a black water bird with a white forehead patch, and a moorhen is a black bird with a red and yellow beak.
exercise: Where is your forehead? | On the back of your neck | *Above your eyes and below your hair | Inside your ear | Under your chin
exercise: «A helmet should sit level and low on your forehead, about two fingers above your eyebrows.» How far above your eyebrows should a helmet sit? | At the very top of your hair | Right on your eyes | About two feet | *About two fingers
exercise: In a story, a character has «sweat on his forehead». What might that show? | Being very happy about a birthday | Feeling full after lunch | A new haircut | *Heat, fear or hard work
test: A coot is a black water bird with a white beak and a white forehead patch. What colour is the coot's forehead patch? | *White | Red and yellow | Black | Green
test: «A wrinkled forehead» can show what? | *Worry or thinking | Being in a swimming pool | Liking cake | Being asleep
exam: «The Qing made men wear the queue, a shaved forehead with a long braid.» In this sentence, what is the queue? | *A shaved forehead with a long braid | A strap under the chin of a helmet | A kind of water bird | A deep bow touching the ground
